       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the dose is still five times the maximum and could seriously harm the patient. I'm not questioning your judgment. A 1000 mg dose of sertraline has no clinical indication I can support.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **If the dose was a typo**, give me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you think the dose is intended**, review it with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist. A dose this far above the maximum should be verified by a licensed prescriber, who can enter it directly. They would also be the ones to set up monitoring.\n- **If the patient has already taken a large amount of sertraline**, that is an overdose, not a prescribing question. Contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or your toxicology service, and escalate to your team now.\n\nI can enter any dose within the recommended range as soon as you tell me which one."
      }
     ],
